    "doi": "https://doi.org/10.1038/nature11789",
    "abstract": null,
    "field": "Paleoclimatology",
    "problem": "Previous efforts to extract a complete Eemian interglacial climate record from Greenland have been unsuccessful because the deep ice layers from this period are consistently disturbed and folded near the bedrock, obscuring the historical climate data and leaving the ice sheet\u2019s response to past warming unclear.",
    "method": "This paper proposes a method to reconstruct the Eemian climate record from a folded Greenland ice core by matching its globally-homogeneous gas and isotope signals to those from dated, undisturbed Antarctic and Greenland ice-core records.",
    "task": "The task is to reconstruct a continuous climate record of the Eemian interglacial period from the disturbed and folded deep layers of the North Greenland Eemian Ice Drilling (NEEM) ice core.",
